INSERT INTO posts (title, slug, content, excerpt, image_url, image_alt, categories, tags, author, wp_id, published, created_at, updated_at, published_at)
VALUES ('Minister Jerry Buttimer opens “In Our Words” social inclusion event in Athlone', 'minister-jerry-buttimer-opens-in-our-words-social-inclusion-event-in-athlone', '<p>See our spread of photos here:</p>
<p><a href="https://www.facebook.com/changingirelandmedia/posts/pfbid022k1Cyq9PwoQgYg2PrqUxQKKbGjCTxvD3HFsmqZM4Uc2WSFQR35Cqj1os4DKMiMjXl?__cft__%5B0%5D=AZVZGwH-woCZ68OWNECu1zL22dSmyP7PiqINHZHNizTk9THriYFWrp-MA2LdiRbdcHD75WhlP2ZJWFKcAgCc7hFvDNvNYntrpUrIZoHoECDWo_lbBUEh5DEtp3tUGFOPRPMC7vK0RMQ-elWy4iA4OlGXcbpCRpI8aPLt9zqSqal8PE8-CGq9t9MrN4vbvBM0w_g&#038;__tn__=%2CO%2CP-R">https://www.facebook.com/changingirelandmedia/posts/pfbid022k1Cyq9PwoQgYg2PrqUxQKKbGjCTxvD3HFsmqZM4Uc2WSFQR35Cqj1os4DKMiMjXl?__cft__%5B0%5D=AZVZGwH-woCZ68OWNECu1zL22dSmyP7PiqINHZHNizTk9THriYFWrp-MA2LdiRbdcHD75WhlP2ZJWFKcAgCc7hFvDNvNYntrpUrIZoHoECDWo_lbBUEh5DEtp3tUGFOPRPMC7vK0RMQ-elWy4iA4OlGXcbpCRpI8aPLt9zqSqal8PE8-CGq9t9MrN4vbvBM0w_g&amp;__tn__=%2CO%2CP-R</a></p>
<p>:</p>
<p>Speaking about the government’s primary social inclusion programme Minister Buttimer TD said, &#8220;Today’s event &#8211; SICAP “In Our Words” is an inspiring showcase of community led social inclusion projects and initiatives, shared through the voices of those with lived experience.&#8221;</p>
<p>The day long gathering celebrated the power of lived experience, bringing together individuals from all parts of Ireland to share their personal journeys and others to highlight the impact of community-led projects supported by the SICAP programme.</p>
<p>The Minister continued:</p>
<p>“Today is about more than just the programme, it is about real people, real stories and the real impact of receiving SICAP supports. I am truly looking forward to hearing about the journeys that brought you here today. By sharing your experiences, you are empowering others to learn, adapt and take meaningful action.”</p>
<p><figure aria-describedby="caption-attachment-255481"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Keynote-Speaker-–-Dr.-Niamh-Sheridan-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1707" srcset="https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Keynote-Speaker-–-Dr.-Niamh-Sheridan-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Keynote-Speaker-–-Dr.-Niamh-Sheridan-300x200.jpg 300w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Keynote-Speaker-–-Dr.-Niamh-Sheridan-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Keynote-Speaker-–-Dr.-Niamh-Sheridan-768x512.jpg 768w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Keynote-Speaker-–-Dr.-Niamh-Sheridan-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Keynote-Speaker-–-Dr.-Niamh-Sheridan-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Keynote-Speaker-–-Dr.-Niamh-Sheridan-1080x720.jpg 1080w" sizes="(max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px" /><figcaption><em>Keynote Speaker – Dr. Niamh Sheridan</em></figcaption></figure></p>
<p>Dr Niamh Sheridan, the keynote speaker; Director of Togher Family Centre in Cork, delivered a truly inspiring speech. Dr Sheridan has worked in community organisations for 25 years and spoke of the power of people in the community to create impactful and far-reaching change.</p>
<p>Niamh said:</p>
<p>“Ireland has a long history of impactful community development. Today’s event has confirmed how deeply we care for each other, and how committed we are as people, to creating a just society for all of those who live in our wonderful country. In the light of the threats to justice and fairness in our world today these characteristics are valuable beyond measure”</p>
<p>Minister Buttimer finished the day by thanking all involved in fostering an equal and inclusive society within marginalised communities.</p>
<p>“Your dedication is making a significant difference, and I eagerly anticipate the positive impact of your future endeavours in continuing to deliver the SICAP programme. Thank you and best wishes for the journey ahead,” he said.</p>
<p>The event concluded with the Chorus Connection Community Choir from Offaly, who performed a medley of songs.</p>
<p>SICAP is co-funded by the Irish Government, through the Department of Rural and Community Development and the Gaeltacht, and the European Social Fund Plus under the Employment, Inclusion, Skills, and Training (EIST) Programme 2021-2027.</p>', 'SICAP beneficiaries and community voices took centre stage today in celebrating the achievements of the Social Inclusion and Community Activation Programme (SICAP) at a showcase event opened by Minister of State with responsibility for Community Development and Charities, Jerry Buttimer. Almost 250 delegates from Local Development Companies, City and County Councils, the Community and Voluntary sector and national representative organisations were in attendance.', 'https://changingireland.ie/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/The-opening-address-was-delivered-by-Minister-of-State-Jerry-Buttimer-scaled.jpg', '', '[{"slug":"development-work","title":"Development Work"}]', '[{"slug":"sicapstories","title":"#SicapStories"},{"slug":"department-of-rural-and-community-development-and-the-gaeltacht","title":"Department of Rural and Community Development and the Gaeltacht"},{"slug":"local-development-companies-network-ldcn","title":"Local Development Companies Network (LDCN)"},{"slug":"minister-jerry-buttimer","title":"Minister Jerry Buttimer"},{"slug":"niamh-sheridan","title":"Niamh Sheridan"},{"slug":"pobal","title":"Pobal"},{"slug":"sicap-social-inclusion-community-activation-programme","title":"SICAP"}]', '', 255477, 1, '2025-10-02T14:51:19Z', '2025-10-23T20:09:05Z', '2025-10-02T14:51:19Z')
